    {
      "data": {
        "text": "<thinking> To create the file `save_audio.py` that writes synthesized speech audio to a local file or object using a concrete external provider, I will use the Amazon Polly service. Amazon Polly is a text-to-speech service that uses advanced deep learning technologies to synthesize speech that sounds like a human voice. I will import the necessary module from the `boto3` library, which is the Amazon Web Services (AWS) SDK for Python. This will make the provider identifiable in the code. </thinking>\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789889566659,
          "start": 1789889564833
        },
        "type": "text"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bdbb50a1001wBArIUIy5UEzJw",
      "message_id": "msg_0bdbb447b001DAosnxrfoEj498",
      "session_id": "ses_f4244bb92ffeW2qsP7EoxSjK4V",
